      <td><code>OBU_BRIDGE_FRAME</code></td>
      <td>SHALL NOT</td>
      <td>MAY</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>OBU_MSDO</code></td>
      <td>SHALL NOT</td>
      <td>MAY</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>OBU_RAS_FRAME</code></td>
      <td>SHALL NOT</td>
      <td>MAY</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>OBU_QUANTIZATION_MATRIX</code></td>
      <td>SHALL NOT</td>
      <td>MAY</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>OBU_FILM_GRAIN</code>, when its contents do not change for the duration of the active [=AV2SampleEntry=]</td>
      <td>MAY</td>
      <td>SHOULD NOT</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>OBU_FILM_GRAIN</code>, otherwise</td>
      <td>SHOULD NOT</td>
      <td>MAY</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>OBU_CONTENT_INTERPRETATION</code></td>
      <td>MAY</td>
      <td>SHALL NOT</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>OBU_PADDING</code></td>
      <td>SHALL NOT</td>
      <td>SHALL NOT (byte-level padding within a track is achieved using ISOBMFF mechanisms, e.g. 'free'/'skip' boxes or <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> size signalling)</td>
     <tr>
  </table>
  <figcaption>List of AV2 OBU types and where they can be found</figcaption>
</figure>

<assert>For a [=Multistream=] bitstream, the [=Sequence Header OBU=] of each extended layer together with the stream's global configuration OBUs SHALL be carried by the associated [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=], in the order specified by the [=ordering of OBUs in a temporal unit=] in [[!AV2]].</assert>

<p class="issue">Editor's note: for a [=Multistream=] bitstream, the [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=] contains a [=Sequence Header OBU=] for each extended layer. The impact on multi-layer use cases — including how a reader determines the active decoder configuration per extended layer from multiple Sequence Header OBUs — needs investigation. Also how profile / level is signalled to decoder API for layers. etc.</p>

## AV2 Sample Format ## {#sample-format}

### General ### {#sample-format-general}

The [=AV2 sample=] boundary delimits the temporal unit.

<assert>Each [=OBU=] within a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> SHALL be framed using the [=Length delimited bitstream format=] specified in Annex B of [[!AV2]]: each OBU is preceded by a <code>leb128()</code> <code>num_bytes_in_obu</code> field giving the byte length of the OBU that follows.</assert> <a class="figure-ref" href="#figure-sample-tu-mapping">Figure</a> illustrates this mapping.

<figure id="figure-sample-tu-mapping">
  <img src="images/av2_sample_tu_mapping.svg" alt="Mapping of AV2 temporal units to ISOBMFF track samples" width="800" height="420">
  <figcaption>Example mapping of AV2 temporal units into the ISOBMFF sample format.</figcaption>
</figure>

### OBUs in samples ### {#sample-obus}

<assert>The [=OBUs=] within a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> SHALL appear in the order specified by the [=ordering of OBUs in a temporal unit=] in [[!AV2]]</assert>, with the following constraint:
- <assert>the [=OBUs=] within a <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l> SHALL NOT contain [=OBUs=] of the types forbidden there as stated in <a class="figure-ref" href="#figure-table-obus">Table</a></assert>.

<p class="issue">Editor's note: the Content Interpretation OBU (<code>OBU_CONTENT_INTERPRETATION</code>) carries picture-level interpretation metadata (for example, colour description) that overlaps ISOBMFF container-level signalling such as the ColourInformationBox. Whether to carry it in the track or replace it entirely with container-level signalling is to be resolved in this version.</p>

### Sync sample ### {#sync-sample}

An [=AV2 sample=] is a <dfn>sync AV2 sample</dfn> if, for every [=coded extended layer unit=] present in the [=AV2 sample=], the first coded frame OBU of that coded extended layer unit has <code>obu_type</code> equal to <code>OBU_CLOSED_LOOP_KEY</code>. Such an [=AV2 sample=] is a [=Closed Random Access=] point for the carried bitstream and corresponds to a SAP of type 1 or 2 as defined in Annex I of [[!ISOBMFF]].

<assert>A [=sync AV2 sample=] SHALL be self-sufficient for starting decoding at that point for all layers: every OBU referenced by the coded frame OBUs of the [=sync AV2 sample=] SHALL be available either by being carried in the [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=] of the active [=AV2SampleEntry=] or by being present in the <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l>, as required by the [=availability of HLS OBUs=] in [[!AV2]].</assert>

NOTE: In ISOBMFF terms, sync samples are signalled using the SyncSampleBox ('stss') in unfragmented tracks, or by setting <code>sample_is_non_sync_sample</code> equal to 0 in fragmented tracks. When every sample in a track is a sync sample, the SyncSampleBox is omitted in unfragmented tracks (per [[!ISOBMFF]]), and in fragmented tracks this is expressed through the default sample flags of the MovieExtendsBox ('trex') or TrackFragmentHeaderBox ('tfhd') with no per-sample override.

### Layers ### {#layers}

The following applies to all [=coded extended layer units=] for each temporal layer in an [=AV2 sample=] associated with a 'pixi' box:
- The channels in the [=AV2 sample=] are considered to be ordered as if the layers were concatenated in increasing <code>xlayer_id</code> order, then in increasing <code>mlayer_id</code> order.
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes the Nth channel as used and specified (<code>channel_idc</code> values other than 0 and 1), the Nth channel in the [=AV2 sample=] SHALL be present.</assert>
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes the Nth channel to be a color channel (<code>channel_idc</code> values such as 2, 3, 4, and 7), the Nth channel in the [=AV2 sample=] SHALL be a color channel: if signalled, the <code>lcr_layer_type</code> field of its associated Layer Configuration Record OBU SHALL be set to 0 (<code>TEXTURE_LAYER</code>).</assert>
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes the Nth channel to be an alpha channel (<code>channel_idc</code> 5), the Nth channel in the [=AV2 sample=] SHALL be an alpha channel: if signalled, the <code>lcr_layer_type</code> field of its associated Layer Configuration Record OBU SHALL be set to 1 (<code>AUX_LAYER</code>) and <code>lcr_auxiliary_type</code> to 0 (<code>ALPHA_AUX</code>).</assert>
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes the Nth channel to be a depth channel (<code>channel_idc</code> 6), the Nth channel in the [=AV2 sample=] SHALL be a depth channel: if signalled, the <code>lcr_layer_type</code> field of its associated Layer Configuration Record OBU SHALL be set to 1 (<code>AUX_LAYER</code>) and <code>lcr_auxiliary_type</code> to 1 (<code>DEPTH_AUX</code>).</assert>
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes the Nth channel as used and specified (<code>channel_idc</code> values other than 0 and 1) with <code>subsampling_flag</code> set to 1, the Nth channel in the [=AV2 sample=] SHALL have the value of the <code>chroma_format_idc</code> field of its associated Sequence Header OBU correspond to the same meaning as the value of the 'pixi' box's Nth channel's <code>subsampling_type</code> value.</assert>
- <assert>If the 'pixi' box describes the Nth channel as used and specified (<code>channel_idc</code> values other than 0 and 1) with <code>subsampling_flag</code> set to 1 and the Nth channel in the [=AV2 sample=] is associated with a Content Interpretation OBU with <code>ci_chroma_sample_position_present_flag</code> set to 1, the value of the <code>ci_chroma_sample_position_top</code> field of that Content Interpretation OBU SHALL correspond to the same meaning as the value of the 'pixi' box's Nth channel's <code>subsampling_location</code> value.</assert>

<div class="example" id="sample-channel-simple-example"><a class="self-link" href="#sample-channel-simple-example"></a>
