### AV2 sample reconstruction ### {#av2-sample-reconstruction}

A byte sequence containing a conformant [[!AV2]] [=Temporal Unit=] using the [=Length delimited bitstream format=] specified in Annex B of [[!AV2]] MAY be reconstructed from the [=OBUs=] of an [=AV2 sample=] by applying the following steps:
1. Write a [=Temporal Delimiter OBU=], preceded by its <code>leb128()</code> length prefix.
2. Write the [=OBUs=] carried in the <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l>, in the same order as present in the <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l>, each preceded by its <code>leb128()</code> length prefix as present in the <l spec=ISOBMFF>[=sample=]</l>.
3. Insert each [=OBU=] carried in the [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=] of the corresponding [=AV2SampleEntry=], preceded by its <code>leb128()</code> length prefix as present in the [=AV2SampleEntry=], between two <code>leb128()</code>-prefixed [=OBUs=] already present in the byte sequence, so that:

    - the relative order of the [=OBUs=] carried in an [=AV2CodecConfigurationBox=] SHALL be kept in the reconstructed byte sequence,
    - the reconstructed byte sequence SHALL conform to the [=ordering of OBUs in a temporal unit=] as specified in [[!AV2]], and
    - there SHALL NOT be an earlier insertion location for that [=OBU=] that would satisfy the above constraints.

Note: AV2-ISOBMFF reader implementations do not have to reconstruct the contiguous byte sequence containing a conformant [=AV2 bitstream=] or [=Temporal Unit=] in memory upon decoding, but they must have all the data to do so: all [=OBUs=], and enough information to deterministically reorder the [=OBUs=] if necessary.

